Why: Check the next visible window, not the next window, when a launched app is minimized to hand the front back: hidden IME and helper windows sit right under it, Windows activates the next visible window, and placing the user's window right under the app is ignored, so a launch refused to hand the front back. The owner route of 0180 now shares the same check.

